\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. With Glorious clouds encompassed round,
\par Whom angels dimly see,
\par Will the Unsearchable be found,
\par Or God appear to me?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Will He forsake His throne above,
\par Himself to me impart?
\par Answer, Thou man of grief and love,
\par And speak it to my heart!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In manifested love explain
\par Thy wonderful design;
\par What meant the suffering Son of Man,
\par The streaming blood divine?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Didst Thou not in our flesh appear,
\par And live and die below,
\par That I may now perceive Thee near,
\par And my Redeemer know?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Come then, and to my soul reveal
\par The heights and depths of grace,
\par The wounds which all my sorrows heal,
\par That dear disfigured face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. I view the Lamb in His own light,
\par Whom angels dimly see,
\par And gaze, transported at the sight,
\par Through all eternity.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

